---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import trailImage from '../assets/images/eucalyptus-trail.png';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Bush Gums"
  description="Why this working hiking brand is simplifying a first overnight setup."
  ><article class="content-page">
    <div class="container narrow prose">
      <span class="eyebrow">About the concept</span><h1>
        Your first setup should feel possible.
      </h1><p class="lead">
        Bush Gums is a temporary working brand for an Australian hiking business
        in validation. The idea is simple: help beginners buy a compatible
        overnight setup without premium-brand prices or a wall of technical
        jargon.
      </p><Image
        class="prose-image"
        src={trailImage}
        alt="A beginner hiker following a eucalyptus bush track in New South Wales"
        widths={[560, 760, 1000]}
        sizes="(max-width: 850px) 100vw, 760px"
        format="webp"
      /><h2>What we are testing</h2><p>
        We are starting with useful guidance, transparent sample kits and a
        decision tool. Over time, that could develop into curated third-party
        kits, affiliate recommendations and eventually thoughtfully specified
        own-brand products.
      </p><h2>How we think about gear</h2><p>
        Lightweight matters because carrying less can make a trip more
        enjoyable. It is one priority among warmth, reliability, comfort and
        cost. We aim to explain those trade-offs clearly, then help people spend
        where it makes a meaningful difference.
      </p><h2>A working brand</h2><p>
        The Bush Gums name and visual identity are placeholders. They are
        centralised in the site configuration so the business can rename and
        restyle the site once customer research gives the brand a firmer
        direction.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article></BaseLayout
>
